{
  "summary": "Moves `m_requested_hb_cmpctblocks`, `m_provides_cmpctblocks`, and `fPreferredDownload` (renamed `m_preferred_download`) from `CNodeState` to `Peer` as atomic variables. It also converts the counter `m_num_preferred_download_peers` to an atomic integer, eliminating `cs_main` locks in several P2P message processing and block relay codepaths.",
  "problem": "Compact block negotiation and preferred download flags in `CNodeState` are protected by `cs_main`, creating unnecessary global lock contention and risks of lock inversion across P2P message handling.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit b3defd44cb notes that protecting these fields with `cs_main` was unnecessary and converting them to atomics avoids 'potential lock inversion in the future or thread safety annotations'",
    "Commit 640f486447 notes that converting `fPreferredDownload` and `m_num_preferred_download_peers` to atomics enables dropping `cs_main` usage in message processing"
  ],
